        "text": "This is the sole remaining local pixel realization repair of the same shared practical bench scene, using the officially closed context and my own directly reviewed saved first result. Preserve the reference-guided woman, the assisting man, the case/continuous shoulder-strap route, two visible fittings, long herringbone coat, knit garment and loafers. The first local result passed grounded soles, bag endpoints, body ownership and reach, but its working forearm covered the required waist/flank gap and its black buckle was already mated. I compare a deep forward lean with a slight upright torso turn and elevated forward work zone: the lean folds fabric across the flank; the upright turn and raised elbows let the coat panel hang outside the torso while the hands present distinct entering components above that gap. Choose the latter. The rigid fork length remains visible between outer-edge grips as only the tips enter the open mouth. The man stabilizes the separate handle and tensions the visible arch while the bench supports the case lower edge; both soles stay flat on the floor. The quiet concentration and softly lit reference-guided face retain the subtle sensual supporting presence at one, with fetish and surreal zero and creativity one limited to local geometry. No new scene, object role, identity, age or body similarity is inferred from either source. The first source preserves the same scene and passed relations; the original attached photograph alone supplies face/hair guidance. These are authorial local staging choices, not new user wording or optional candidate meanings.",
